# Docker context for `langgraph build` is this directory (langgraph_cli sets the build
# context to langgraph.json's parent, then `ADD`s the lot), so what is listed here is what
# stays out of the deploy image. Nothing else reads this file — local runs are unaffected.
#
# The entries that matter are the two big ones: .chat-ui (the dev-only Next frontend,
# node_modules included) and data/ (20M+ of fetched abstracts, re-fetchable and
# machine-local). .venv too — the image builds its own from uv.lock, and a macOS venv
# would be wrong in a Linux image even if it were small.
#
# `**/` on anything that can appear at depth: unlike .gitignore, a bare `node_modules/`
# here matches only the context root, so ui/node_modules would otherwise ship.
#
# Do NOT add pyproject.toml, uv.lock, langgraph.json, research_agent/, ui/ or README.md:
# the first four are the build inputs, ui/ is the artifact components the graph bundles,
# and pyproject declares `readme = "README.md"`, so excluding it fails the build outright.
.chat-ui/
# Frontend sources for that same dev-only app; setup copies them into .chat-ui/src.
chat-ui-overlay/
.venv/
data/
.git/
.github/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[oc]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.langgraph_api/
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets stay on the host. langgraph.json's `env` becomes docker-compose's `env_file`,
# read at run time from outside the image, so the file itself is never needed in here.
.env

# Measures the agent rather than being part of it, and nothing shipped should carry a test
# framework (see CLAUDE.md on why evals/ sits outside the package). Safe to drop because
# [tool.setuptools] names the packages explicitly and the version is static — the build
# reads neither evals/ nor .git/.
evals/
